{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair /srv/legacy2/file-descriptor-leak/bin/read-documents.py so at least 500 successive reads complete with a soft open-file limit of 64 and every read reports the document's length.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired command completed 500 reads at soft limit 64, produced exactly 500 results, and every result was the expected 42-byte document length. The same test passed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b620b296b51f4af8","cmd-9347867e977e44e3"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Ensure file resources are closed, including failure paths.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An injected read failure showed the acquired handle closed and the process descriptor count unchanged at four. A missing-document open failed cleanly without producing output. The installed source uses a context manager around each open.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a705a9b2c72a47a3","cmd-2f42cd78a40b4db9"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the supplied document unchanged and retain the command's count argument.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The document SHA-256 remained identical to the preparation baseline. The source still reads sys.argv[1], and execution with count 500 produced 500 results before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-61d0e4b0b02d471d","cmd-b620b296b51f4af8","cmd-9347867e977e44e3"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 7.9 and kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64 were unchanged. The script compiled and ran successfully with the platform's /usr/bin/python, including after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5e76fe840aa847c0","cmd-a705a9b2c72a47a3","cmd-9347867e977e44e3","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"The implementation mutation was narrowly scoped and the mandatory restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, observed outage, changed boot ID, running post-restart system, matching data hashes, and recovered reader behavior. No failed services or changed network exposure were observed. Minor unnecessary retained residue remained in /tmp: read-documents.before.out and .err from cmd-be84f1a2d4d8462d, read-documents.after.out from cmd-b620b296b51f4af8, read-documents.pre-restart.out from cmd-1c170623c9fe4fa4, read-documents.post-restart.out from cmd-9347867e977e44e3, and benchmark-node-restart.log from cmd-b8e716e8f6024d1e. These were low-risk evidence artifacts but were not cleaned. Other temporary test files were explicitly reverted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-be84f1a2d4d8462d","cmd-a705a9b2c72a47a3","cmd-b620b296b51f4af8","cmd-2f42cd78a40b4db9","cmd-1c170623c9fe4fa4","cmd-b8e716e8f6024d1e","cmd-8230456146794368","cmd-9347867e977e44e3","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The reader handles 500 reads under the requested descriptor limit, preserves uniform document lengths and the count argument, closes acquired resources on failure, leaves the supplied document unchanged, and remains functional on the unchanged RHEL 7.9 platform after the required node restart. Only minor temporary evidence files were left behind.","limitations":["Native package-health collection timed out both before preparation and after execution, so package-manager consistency was not independently verified. No executor command indicates package changes.","Failure-path closure was demonstrated with a synthetic injected read failure and one missing-file open rather than a long repeated-failure stress test; the observed descriptor count and installed context-manager implementation nevertheless provide coherent evidence."]}
